Package: librowise
Version: @VERSION@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @PYTHON@, libc6, passwd, ca-certificates
Recommends: postgresql (>= 14), postgresql-client, caddy | nginx, logrotate, curl
Suggests: certbot, python3-certbot-nginx
Homepage: https://github.com/librowise/librowise
Description: modern, AI-assisted integrated library system (Koha replacement)
 Librowise is a library management system: catalogue with MARC21 and
 authorities, circulation, holds, fines, OPAC, serials, course reserves,
 acquisitions suggestions, reports, SIP2 for self-check machines, SRU and
 OAI-PMH, with optional Claude-powered AI assistance.
 .
 This package installs the application into a self-contained Python
 environment under /opt/librowise, the `librowise` command and systemd
 template units. Create a library with `librowise instance create`, which
 sets up a PostgreSQL database, the services and an HTTPS reverse proxy,
 like koha-create does for Koha.
